The test method directly calls `fig.get_tightbbox(renderer)` twice, once before `fig.tight_layout(...)` and once after, so the counted `Figure.get_tightbbox` returns are 2. The oracle parser also sets `tight_layout_traced` to true whenever it sees any traced line event from `matplotlib._tight_layout.get_tight_layout_figure`, and it extracts `pos`, `tight_bbox`, `h_pad`, and `w_pad` only for events whose `_tight_layout.py` line numbers fall in 180–219. Using that parser contract together with the recorded runtime values for this test case yields the first bbox and the listed constraint variables.

